From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shutdown: shutdown.exe shuts down, restarts and signs out

Wine's shutdown.exe was a stub that printed its arguments. It now takes
/s /r /g /p /l /h /a /f /t /c /d as Windows does and calls ExitWindowsEx
(which wine-sg 0241 hands to logind) or SetSuspendState. Delays run in the
process, so /a has nothing to abort. Gate: make test-shutdownexe.
---
--- a/programs/shutdown/Makefile.in
+++ b/programs/shutdown/Makefile.in
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 MODULE    = shutdown.exe
+IMPORTS   = user32 powrprof
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -mconsole -municode
 
--- a/programs/shutdown/main.c
+++ b/programs/shutdown/main.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 /*
